    "note": "Q408318/way382655135 identifies the wider site. Sixteen actual normal-map roof footprints identify the principal halls and gallery arms; point controls17598413339131/17598413339130/17596588194605 place Dabotap, Seokgatap and the sarira stupa. The ordinary visitor-style layout guides names and relative courts, while current PMTiles geometry controls metric positions. Raw east/south coordinates retain the signed front approach; the main hall east axis is9.67 degrees north of east. Concave gallery roof ribbons are rectified within approximately55cm to suppress sub-metre map jitter; original control vertices remain unchanged in source. Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged 161-square/6m standard DEM. Sixteen mapped halls retain raw east/south coordinates; the main hall east axis is9.67 degrees north of east and the stairs face the southern approach. Individual court levels step up the hillside. Twenty-seven occupied floor pockets merge to ten level meshes, each with a complete opaque top and continuous retaining foundation. Entrance bridge walks have inward cut-bank joins to the coarse DEM. First-render foundation gaps were corrected; the open stone vault remains real geometry. These buried joins and court/threshold levels are visualization estimates, not surveyed basement walls. Only bounded occupied floors open ground; sixteen individual guarded roof envelopes replace authored buildings. All115 independent source-map records were checked outside these envelopes. Full-site loading replaces16 authored roofs and preserves42 independent tile buildings exactly. Three native water features retain19263.106301357795 square metres. Failure keeps all58 native tile buildings and terrain; eviction restores surfaces and frees geometry. Synthetic64m residency clips the architecture, including part of the entrance bridge, and retains the existing temporary-boundary contact limitation. Partial architectural completeness/contact is not approved. Only the portable source preview seats terrain under authored floors; production uses the unmodified retained grid. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
  },
